    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense, but i'm still seeing these sudden, almost \"aggressive\" spikes in acidity that don't seem to follow a linear progression with the temp. it feels like the microbial activity isn't just speeding up, but almost behaving erratically or acting out for no reason. is there any specific biological mechanism where the bacteria might suddenly go into a hyper-active state like that?",
