      "content": "Yes, the microbial community's internal dynamics can become unpredictable even with seemingly controlled inputs. Starters are complex ecosystems, and an imbalance in fungal-to-bacterial ratios or the presence of trace contaminants can throw the entire system into flux. Sometimes, the starter reaches a state of over-competition where different species out-compete or inhibit each other erratically, leading to sudden surges. Consider doing a strict \"reset\" period, perhaps long rests, to see if the community settles into a more stable equilibrium.",
